Xvoid ConfigScreenMgr(int force, ResType theType, int theID,
X	int (*configProc)(Handle theData));
X
XA routine to manipulate resources in the configuration file.  Checks for the presence of the resource indicated by theType and theID.  If this resource is not found, it does nothing.  If the resource is found somewhere other than in the configuration file (see InitScreenMgr()), this routine assumes that some action needs to be taken.  The usual place other the the configuration file to find this kind of resource is in the program file itself and logically represents default values.  If some action needs t





o be taken or force is non-zero, the routine pointed to by configProc is called.  TheData contains a handle to the resource found as described above.  ConfigProc should generally put up a dialog box to change the data in theHandle.  If it does change the data, configProc should return true.  Otherwise, false.  If configProc returns true, the handle is marked changed so that it is added to the configuration file.  A nice time to call this routine is at the start of your program with force false, so that ini





tiXal configuration information can be obtained from the user.  Then provide a menu item in the application menu to allow the user to change it later, calling this routine with force true.
