Xint PushScreen();
X
XSaves the current screen buffer (characters, attributes, and cursor location) on a stack.  Allocates a significant amount of memory.  Returns 0 if successful.
X
Xvoid PopScreen()
X
XSets the screen contents to the last screen saved by PushScreen().  If there are no saved screens on the stack, does nothing.
